700	  // The named functions are the ones whose signature is dangerous the moment it
701	  // is reachable from the network: they take a caller-supplied id or secret and
702	  // deliberately carry no auth of their own, because their callers are supposed
703	  // to have done it. Re-exporting any of them from a "use server" file recreates
704	  // the original incident exactly.
