735	/* ================================================================== *
736	 * The rate-limit key was a field the caller filled in
737	 *
738	 * nginx forwards `X-Forwarded-For: $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`, which APPENDS
739	 * the peer it saw to whatever the caller sent. So the LEFTMOST entry is
740	 * caller-authored text, and `(xff ?? "").split(",")[0]` — the expression that
741	 * keyed the login, register, password-reset, verification-resend and wallet
742	 * top-up throttles — returns whatever the caller typed.
743	 *
